caseprompts={4:('A genetic counseling learner confuses whether a trait appears with how strongly it appears.','Explain penetrance versus expressivity and use the supplied variation in neurofibromatosis as your comparison.','Penetrance describes the fraction expressing a phenotype. Expressivity describes variation among people with the genotype. The supplied neurofibromatosis example varies from skin spots to more extensive disease.','4:43,44'),5:('Two surveys use the same town: one measures new diagnoses over a year; the other measures all affected people on one date.','Explain why the two results cannot be labeled with the same epidemiologic measure.','The first measures incidence over an interval; the second measures prevalence at a point in time. Relative risk would require comparable incidence in exposed and unexposed groups.','5:5,6'),6:('A gene sequence is unchanged, but its promoter becomes heavily methylated.','Explain the expected expression change and distinguish it from deletion of the gene.','Promoter methylation can reduce transcription while leaving the DNA sequence present. Deletion removes genetic material. Epigenetic regulation changes expression.','6:4,29'),12:('A cancer cell leaves a primary mass and enters circulation, but no distant colony develops.','Explain why entry into circulation does not alone complete metastasis.','The cell must cross tissue barriers, survive transport and survive and proliferate in a receptive distant environment. Proteases aid matrix/basement-membrane passage.','12:38,39,40'),13:('Two people share an exposure but differ in DNA repair, inflammatory activity and metabolism.','Use the packet to explain why exposure alone cannot fix an individual outcome.','The source includes genetic, epigenetic, local tissue, immune and metabolic contributors. Similar exposure need not imply identical susceptibility.','13:5,6'),14:('A learner treats every childhood tumor as an adult epithelial tumor occurring early.','Contrast the supplied developmental and tissue-origin framework with that assumption.','The deck emphasizes mesodermal origins and embryonal tumors from immature tissue. Embryonal tumors begin prenatally; this developmental category cannot be reduced to an adult epithelial pattern.','14:4,6'),46:('A healed wound becomes raised and firm. Another lesion is a pressure injury with a covered base.','Explain which additional observation distinguishes a keloid from a hypertrophic scar, and why the covered pressure injury cannot be staged from depth alone.','Extension beyond the original wound favors keloid; hypertrophic scars remain within it. A base covered by slough/eschar is unstageable until depth can be assessed.','46:29,31,32'),47:('An infant has itchy eczema. Later a wet diaper area develops sharply bounded satellite lesions.','Separate barrier/inflammatory disease from the new infectious complication.','Atopic dermatitis involves barrier and immune dysfunction. Satellite pustulovesicular lesions in diaper dermatitis support secondary Candida involvement in the supplied notes.','47:9,10,12,61N'),48:('An extensively burned adult has tissue swelling while intravascular volume is inadequate.','Explain the apparent contradiction and identify the supplied resuscitation monitor without repeating the disputed released explanation.','Edema and intravascular depletion can coexist after fluid shifts and loss. Replacement restores circulating volume; urine output monitors adequacy. Increasing permeability is not the supported purpose.','48:46,48,54'),49:('A child has poor perfusion with normal systolic pressure; another has an age-related risk of high evaporative losses after burns.','Explain why normal pressure does not exclude shock and why burn replacement needs differ with body proportions.','Compensated shock may preserve pressure despite impaired perfusion. Greater surface area relative to weight increases evaporative water loss in children.','49:5,6,18,53')}
